#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-esc-calibration.rst:4
#: a799574c1d794b8da806bc8814d228d9
msgid "ESC calibration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-esc-calibration.rst:6
#: a0293da93305455db8de763366d18ccb
msgid "Most models of PWM based ESC (not DShot ESCs) need to be calibrated to ensure that all the ESCs respond to the same input with the same speed. To calibrate them they need to receive maximum PWM input when initially powered on, then receive minimum PWM input when they have beeped to indicate that the maximum has registered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-esc-calibration.rst:12
#: cdf21e816b234e19bd4c9ddb1b8c85fc
msgid "if ESC RPM telemetry is being used, the :ref:`TKOFF_RPM_MIN <TKOFF_RPM_MIN>` parameter could be set slightly below the :ref:`Q_M_SPIN_ARM <Q_M_SPIN_ARM>` parameter to prevent takeoff attempts, and subsequent flips on takeoff, if one or more motors are not spinning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-esc-calibration.rst:15
#: 89da9d92c01c4830a98e8747c61faf3e
msgid "You must remove all propellers from your vehicle before doing any ESC calibration. Calibrating with propellers installed is dangerous."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-esc-calibration.rst:19
#: ab0a3f1e28e7466f94f000e3b4b40d10
msgid "ESC Calibration Procedure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-esc-calibration.rst:20
#: 069cc77a5927495880b63541b1a4ca29
msgid "This process uses the :ref:`Q_ESC_CAL <Q_ESC_CAL>` parameter to enable ESC calibration in QSTABILIZE mode. There are two modes of operation available:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-esc-calibration.rst:24
#: d3a85d5928ce4560947d47b4d4d4329e
msgid "with Q\\_ESC_CAL=1 the output to the motors will come directly from the throttle stick in QSTABILIZE mode when the vehicle is armed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-esc-calibration.rst:26
#: 096e147779bb43fcbdb3f81693b40b88
msgid "with Q\\_ESC_CAL=2 the output to the motors will be full throttle when the motors are armed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-esc-calibration.rst:29
#: de368ca8a27c4b8a803b6d2f3dc52bd2
msgid "The process when using Q\\_ESC_CAL=1 is"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-esc-calibration.rst:31
#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-esc-calibration.rst:50
#: 07b6233dd0744d6cb76257fe4806995b
#: 268a8b37ed5c4d79b886bbdd0d2539ac
msgid "remove your propellers for safety"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-esc-calibration.rst:32
#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-esc-calibration.rst:51
#: 639824fe6d7b408e96e25d999b290a1b
#: 3864b293cf754f79bb817e22d1bbcf3c
msgid "power up just the flight board and not your motors. If you don't have the ability to isolate power to the ESCs when on battery power then power up your flight board on USB power"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-esc-calibration.rst:35
#: c7a821aecfe84153afd866cbfba74f16
msgid "set the Q\\_ESC_CAL parameter to 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-esc-calibration.rst:36
#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-esc-calibration.rst:55
#: 6ae87951cdc74904b8a242150655ecd3
#: 602aecaf053248469f45e2c54be96581
msgid "change to QSTABILIZE mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-esc-calibration.rst:37
#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-esc-calibration.rst:56
#: 9d09d95932bf4534905adbccad7528c0
#: bd07e665c8b74fef974446f8a187e8a0
msgid "set the safety switch off to activate the outputs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-esc-calibration.rst:38
#: 466811b84e8948d8b166547328f9708a
msgid "arm your aircraft. The PWM output on all quad motors will now be controlled by your throttle stick"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-esc-calibration.rst:40
#: 0dbc4979bb794d0ab35ad53e5b214575
msgid "move the throttle stick to maximum"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-esc-calibration.rst:41
#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-esc-calibration.rst:58
#: e1b9b5d9e8a2490e8e3c9ed690084eaf
#: aa28c62876454e31b0a94ddd7ec00cdb
msgid "add power to your ESCs by connecting the battery"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-esc-calibration.rst:42
#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-esc-calibration.rst:59
#: 2427227ae77f4e9fbeeff4be1066910a
#: 10de50abfda7404e96ff29074f6dd212
msgid "wait for the ESCs to beep to indicate they have registered the maximum PWM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-esc-calibration.rst:44
#: fd740b39688d4813b8c4ac2e9eb8cd58
msgid "lower the throttle stick to zero and disarm your aircraft"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-esc-calibration.rst:45
#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-esc-calibration.rst:62
#: 50c32a5ff1aa4ea3b3884b967963fa5f
#: 103c120d6f8043b1a08838a50090e294
msgid "you should hear a beep from your ESCs to indicate they have registered the throttle range"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-esc-calibration.rst:48
#: 22a8d05d7f3e4d1c98fae9f89decad6f
msgid "The process when using Q\\_ESC\\_CAL=2 is"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-esc-calibration.rst:54
#: 310fb118ba2f44c596b470bd303b2eb3
msgid "set the Q\\_ESC_CAL parameter to 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-esc-calibration.rst:57
#: 817cf2e5f6684cd499fd369134b6fc76
msgid "arm your aircraft. The PWM output on all quad motors will now be at maximum"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-esc-calibration.rst:61
#: b856958a00604cdfa8624cff460ae53a
msgid "disarm your aircraft"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-esc-calibration.rst:65
#: c37d1e11bce94d3ea40e81ad8a5b04f5
msgid "Note that using Q\\_ESC_CAL=1 can be useful for testing your motors response. This is the only mode when you are able to directly control the throttle level on all your motors at once. While in this mode you can use a laser tachometer to test your motor speeds at different throttle levels if you have one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-esc-calibration.rst:71
#: 42bb0d551b884da6a50256c613963dce
msgid "Be sure to set :ref:`Q_ESC_CAL<Q_ESC_CAL>` back to zero after calibrating for normal operation"
msgstr ""
